ntion), puts concern for others (crew), keeps calm in crisis (stress resilience). Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (crew), not willing further education (adaptability). So strong on many core criteria, but communication issues.\n\nD: Responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence, decision quality), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: moody, loner (crew cooperation, communication). No data on reliability, but responsibility suggests maturity.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. C seems strong across many criteria, but communication difficulty could be serious. However, crew cooperation is positive. B has reliability and stress but crew cooperation issues. D has problem solving and responsibility but crew issues. A lacks many data.\n\nThus likely C is best overall, despite communication concerns, because crew cooperation and decision quality are crucial. Also C's concern for others and positive atmosphere may mitigate communication difficulty. Also C's attention and quick correct decisions are strong.\n\nThus Emily should vote for Candidate C, perhaps supporting James, but also bring up D or A for completeness. She can ask for more info on D's crew cooperation or A's reliability. But need to keep one focused contribution. She could say she agrees with James, but wants to probe D's crew cooperation before final. However she must give a vote now. She can vote for C, but note need more info on D and A.\n\nThus public message: agree with James, support C, reference facts: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention, but note concerns about communication and egocentric but still overall stronger than B's uncooperative and A's unfriendly. Provide reasoning.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
